{"kind":"report","text":"Approved for request 5d41ea36aa0047fbd9e285e3276188e0f3b9131b / builder promise 9c75aae2fbdac4fd0fba800aa3a21eeba10f9bf8 at exact 87cd5804218bcf59cf69a849743d4ccbb8a66cce. Primary 7f31fd6958287af4585a9bc4a060ba346d405389 is first, with all six submitted artifacts. Each is individually effective and directly based on the builder promise; I independently verified exact commit/path/blob/byte/SHA256 identities, totaling 1,107,255 UTF-8 bytes. The complete delta from 736f4953 is exactly those six paths, with requests.ts the only Room source change. The full original request, invitation, report and source/test/contract delta were read.\n\nCondition 1 is explicitly decided: planner assertion a6e9a14a57f6836063c38e37d319570ccadbd72b accepts the exact R-CRED-10 paragraph semantically. Root read and verified it effective. Unknown/expired token, revoked session key, invalid/expired delegation, revoked grantor key for any reason, or inactive member ends bearer access. Reads, bearer acts and bearer requests use the same judgment. Role or declared-kind changes remain current new-act admission checks. This acceptance does not itself supply runtime proof.\n\nThe source meets that rule: requests.ts472–486 retains the bearer-only lookup and held-seed requirement, and calls authenticateHash before signing or dispatching. authenticateHash186–196 includes the previously missing grantor revocation and active-member checks. Both bearerAct496 and bearerRequest558 use it. The judgment is synchronous before either operation proceeds. HTTP MCP already authenticated through the read path; the demonstrated prior inconsistency concerned direct RoomWire bearer calls and exact retry disclosure, not a new-effect or HTTP admission bypass.\n\nIndependent bounded execution supports the repair. The shipped real-Room witness 'a bearer session ends with its grantor' passes: 1 executed passed, 44 unselected, exit 0, 2.389s. It retires the grantor key while explicitly proving the delegation itself remains unrevoked; HTTP MCP listing returns 401, direct exact bearer retry and workspace request are unauthenticated, and no entry is recorded. A saved signed envelope from the original log still settles to its original receipt. A separate removed member's session is likewise rejected. The actual Room runs in local workerd/SQLite with the existing policy and fake Artifacts/checker/publisher seams; there is no provider or deployed-runtime credit.\n\nOne hand-made control restores only the old judgeBearer in an owned scratch checkout. The same unchanged witness fails at worker.test.ts1105 with a loaded AssertionError, 'expected a failure, got' the original receipt: 0 passed, 1 failed, 44 unselected, exit 1, 2.175s. No timeout or setup failure is treated as distinction. Tests and configuration stayed unchanged. Root vetted the full control diff, raw executed statuses, eight saved evidence hashes and twelve exact source/fixture identities. All 711 tracked fixture files were independently checked against the saved before hashes after restoration, with no mismatch. Evidence: /var/folders/2x/wylr59t17ds36l1l7ng25y7w0000gn/T/artroom-checker-bearer-87cd-1r2tnaie; manifest SHA256 74652211c61f11fe10a6d7688fb528bc91ca0d6fd66d54ebca740fc26617bc16.\n\nThe changed existing response-loss recovery case also passes separately through the shipped roster-and-redemption workerd wrapper: 1 executed passed, 68 unselected, exit 0, 2.156s. It checks the retired stranded session is unauthenticated and the fresh replacement can still act. Root verified the wrapper against exact Git bytes, both saved output hashes and the raw executed assertion. Separate follow-up manifest SHA256 b41681c53325c43e6b8dc165c809b7bc72bc051d007d91524cd3c8a629868f59. This is additional bounded evidence, not a relabelled run of the first witness/control.\n\nSaved signed settlement remains compatible by source and actual witness. admission.ts verifies the signature before its exact idempotency return at359–360, which precedes current new-act authority at370–371. Its acceptedBefore path224–230 preserves historical-shape exact retries. This repair grants no current read/bearer permission from an old signed envelope and repeats no recorded effect. The role/kind distinction is source-reviewed rather than credited with new runtime cases here.\n\nArchitecture: sharing credential judgment removes the diverging read/act/request paths while retaining endpoint-specific bearer custody. Security: current bearer access ends with its grantor/member, and independently authenticated saved signed bytes settle their historical result. Simplification: reuse authenticateHash instead of maintaining another revocation/member checklist; keep current access and idempotent settlement separate.\n\nThe clean exact checkout passes git diff --check for the complete delta. Builder's exact-head 2,032-test gate is recorded evidence; this review did not rerun the broad gate or contact providers. The changed requests.ts dependency is explicitly reviewed here after Stage 2's 39430e23 approval, whose core remains unchanged; that earlier approval is not automatically extended to this whole head. Stage 5's pending capacity/UI/authenticated-entry changes, Stage 3's complete accounting, MCP's disjoint output integration and final original-contract/runtime dual binding remain separate. This approval covers the complete five conditions of 5d41, not final branch composition or deployment. Identity inventory: /var/folders/2x/wylr59t17ds36l1l7ng25y7w0000gn/T/artroom-bearer-87cd-identity-qh_07vvq.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f31fd6958287af4585a9bc4a060ba346d405389","binding":"assigned","head":"87cd5804218bcf59cf69a849743d4ccbb8a66cce","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a6e9a14a57f6836063c38e37d319570ccadbd72b\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bc0b176a97f9d8f2d4408a6737efa194